Problem link : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/delete-all-occurrences-of-a-given-key-in-a-doubly-linked-list/1

class Solution:
    def deleteAllOccurOfX(self, head, x):
        curr = head
        while curr:
            nxt = curr.next
            if curr.data == x:
                if curr.prev:
                    curr.prev.next = curr.next
                else:
                    head = curr.next  # deleting head node
                if curr.next:
                    curr.next.prev = curr.prev
            curr = nxt
        return head

'''
    Time complexity : O(n) — single pass through the list
    Space complexity: O(1) — only pointer variables, no extra data structures
    
    Traverse the DLL once. For each node matching x, unlink it by
    rewiring prev/next pointers. Handle head deletion by advancing head.
